ather because we are importing a single type (number) into two types (int/float), so users can no longer do things like check if the type of two values match and get the same result that JSON would indicate (`true` for comparing int/flost literals for type equality).","created_at":"2026-01-31T01:36:14Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T01:36:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114872#discussion_r2748657839","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114872","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2748657839"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114872#discussion_r2748657839"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114872"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2748657839/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":34,"original_line":34,"side":"LEFT","in_reply_to_id":2747102483,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2749684214","pull_request_review_id":3732897447,"id":2749684214,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6j5Nn2","diff_hunk":"@@ -31,7 +31,6 @@\n \t\t[b]Note:[/b] Both parse methods do not fully comply with the JSON specification:\n \t\t- Trailing commas in arrays or objects are ignored, instead of causing a parser error.\n \t\t- New line and tab characters are accepted in string literals, and are treated like their corresponding escape sequences [code]\\n[/code] and [code]\\t[/code].\n-\t\t- Numbers are parsed using [method String.to_float] which is generally more lax than the JSON specification.","path":"doc/classes/JSON.xml","commit_id":"507df6996a7dcd0c0c9135d70762c47b3fe33339","original_commit_id":"a9b67c6e8d088bcde7d9dce336fb0995b8d3d4f8","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I wouldn't consider using two types to represent numbers non-compliance, so I'd rather not have it in the section for non-compliance with the JSON spec. There is no restriction that our representation needs to match the types or structure from the JSON text grammar.\r\n\r\nActually I don't think any of these notes here are non-compliant, they are saying we are less strict than required, which is allowed. `A JSON parser MAY accept non-JSON forms or extensions.`\r\nMaybe I should change it to say `Both parse methods are less strict than the JSON spec`?\r\n\r\nI figured out what the original note referred to, its for numbers like `-01 and -2. and 0.e1 and 2.e+3 and 2.e-3 and 2.e3 and -.123` which is more lenient than the spec. (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/66114)\r\n\r\nAnd I was going to adjust the message to:\r\n`Numbers with only the integer component are parsed as integers when possible, and as floats otherwise.`","created_at":"2026-01-31T15:37:47Z","updated_at":"2026-01-31T15:37:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114872#discussion_r2749684214","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114872","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2749684214"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114872#discussion_r2749684214"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114872"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2749684214/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":34,"original_line":34,"side":"LEFT","in_reply_to_id":2747102483,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2783878421","pull_request_review_id":3774607254,"id":2783878421,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6l7p0V","diff_hunk":"@@ -31,7 +31,6 @@\n \t\t[b]Note:[/b] Both parse methods do not fully comply with the JSON specification:\n \t\t- Trailing commas in arrays or objects are ignored, instead of causing a parser error.\n \t\t- New line and tab characters are accepted in string literals, and are treated like their corresponding escape sequences [code]\\n[/code] and [code]\\t[/code].\n-\t\t- Numbers are parsed using [method String.to_float] which is generally more lax than the JSON specification.","path":"doc/classes/JSON.xml","commit_id":"507df6996a7dcd0c0c9135d70762c47b3fe33339","original_commit_id":"a9b67c6e8d088bcde7d9dce336fb0995b8d3d4f8","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/use