sed using [method String.to_float] or [method String.to_int] which are generally more lax than the JSON specification. For example, numbers such as [code]-01[/code], [code]-2.[/code], [code]2.e+3[/code], and [code]-.123[/code] are considered valid.`","created_at":"2026-04-07T16:56:44Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T16:56:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114872#discussion_r3046611815","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114872","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3046611815"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114872#discussion_r3046611815"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114872"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3046611815/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":34,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3045477569,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":8,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3046612246","pull_request_review_id":4069895283,"id":3046612246,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc61l50W","diff_hunk":"@@ -78,6 +78,7 @@\n \t\t\t\tReturns an [enum Error]. If the parse was successful, it returns [constant OK] and the result can be retrieved using [member data]. If unsuccessful, use [method get_error_line] and [method get_error_message] to identify the source of the failure.\n \t\t\t\tNon-static variant of [method parse_string], if you want custom error handling.\n \t\t\t\tThe optional [param keep_text] argument instructs the parser to keep a copy of the original text. This text can be obtained later by using the [method get_parsed_text] function and is used when saving the resource (instead of generating new text from [member data]).\n+\t\t\t\t[b]Note:[/b] Numbers with only the integer component are parsed as integers when possible, and as floats otherwise.","path":"doc/classes/JSON.xml","commit_id":"e76ac9a85ccb2fbc73883f3033cd65bc306d1bdc","original_commit_id":"31237258603f801af3cb328eaed98f59504c3a82","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The above note is specifically about the ways that parsing is more lax than the spec, and this one is about how numbers are determined to be ints vs floats. So they convey 2 different things, I don't think its redundant.","created_at":"2026-04-07T16:56:50Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T16:56:50Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114872#discussion_r3046612246","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114872","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3046612246"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114872#discussion_r3046612246"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114872"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://ap